.TH GRIDFORGE 1 "November 2026" "GridForge 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
GridForge \- meshing and simulation workbench
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B GridForge
.RI [ STUDY ]
.br
.B GridForge
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
GridForge takes a part's geometry, meshes it, sets up its materials,
loads and supports, solves it through an installable toolkit (CalculiX
first), and shows how it responds. Results leave as files for ParaView.
.PP
The banner at the top of the window always says the next step.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I STUDY
A study folder (one holding a study.json) to open.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and the build, and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I study.json
A study: its geometry, mesh recipe, solve and set-up.
.TP
.I <part>.brep, <part>.groups.json
A part from FreeCAD with its named groups, as GridForge's FreeCAD macro
writes them (File, New Study from Geometry; then Study, Add Groups From
FreeCAD).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gf-study (1)
